Here's the code to insert at the top of the Food page:

```html
<div class="safety-alert-callout" style="background-color: #ff0000; color: white; padding: 15px; margin: 10px 0; border-radius: 5px; font-weight: bold; text-align: center;">
  <span style="font-size: 1.2em;">⚠️ SAFETY ALERT:</span> High-crime activity reported near red-tagged establishments. Avoid these areas after dark based on historical neighborhood demographics.
</div>
```

Or, if you prefer a more maintainable CSS approach:

```html
<div class="safety-alert-callout">
  <span class="alert-icon">⚠️ SAFETY ALERT:</span> High-crime activity reported near red-tagged establishments. Avoid these areas after dark based on historical neighborhood demographics.
</div>

<style>
.safety-alert-callout {
  background-color: #ff0000;
  color: white;
  padding: 15px;
  margin: 10px 0;
  border-radius: 5px;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-align: center;
}

.alert-icon {
  font-size: 1.2em;
}
</style>
```

To implement this:

1. Locate the HTML file for the Food page
2. Insert the code immediately after the opening `<body>` tag or within the main content area at the top
3. If using the CSS approach, place the `<style>` block in the `<head>` section or your existing stylesheet

